{"level": "Elementary", "number": 99, "title": "A2 Mock 2 \u2014 Reading and Writing", "passages": {}, "layout": "<div class=\"booklet\"><p style=\"margin-bottom:2px\"><span style=\"font-weight:700;color:#127D80;font-size:9pt\">A2 KEY \u00b7 MOCK FINAL</span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:6px\"><span style=\"font-weight:700;color:#0B5456;font-size:20pt\">Reading and Writing</span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:8px\"><span style=\"font-style:italic;color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">Five parts, twenty-five questions, and one email. Answer every question \u2014 a wrong answer costs nothing.</span></p><table class=\"bk\"><tr><td style=\"background:#127D80;width:92px;border:0;vertical-align:middle\"><p style=\"text-align:center;margin:0\"><span style=\"font-weight:700;color:#fff;font-size:11pt\">PART 1</span></p></td><td style=\"border:0;border-bottom:1px solid #127D80;vertical-align:middle\"><p style=\"margin:0\"><span style=\"font-weight:700;color:#0B5456;font-size:11pt\">Questions 1\u20135 \u00b7 the notices</span></p></td></tr></table><p style=\"margin-bottom:8px\"><span style=\"font-style:italic;color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">Which notice (A-H) says this (1-5)? For questions 1 to 5, mark the correct letter A-H on the answer sheet.</span></p><table class=\"bk\"><tr><td style=\"background:#F2F8F8;border:1px solid #127D80;padding:10px 12px\"><p style=\"margin-bottom:4px\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\"><b>A</b> &nbsp;PLEASE LEAVE YOUR BAGS AT THE DESK</span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:4px\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\"><b>B</b> &nbsp;NO PARKING IN FRONT OF THESE DOORS</span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:4px\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\"><b>C</b> &nbsp;THIS MACHINE DOES NOT GIVE CHANGE</span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:4px\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\"><b>D</b> &nbsp;SWIMMING POOL CLOSED FOR CLEANING</span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:4px\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\"><b>E</b> &nbsp;CHILDREN UNDER 12 MUST BE WITH AN ADULT</span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:4px\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\"><b>F</b> &nbsp;LAST TRAIN LEAVES AT 11.30 P.M.</span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:4px\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\"><b>G</b> &nbsp;PLEASE DO NOT WALK ON THE GRASS</span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:4px\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\"><b>H</b> &nbsp;STAFF ONLY - DO NOT ENTER</span></p></td></tr></table><p style=\"margin-bottom:6px;padding-left:16px\"><span style=\"color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">1</span> <span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">You must bring the right money for this.</span> <span data-mcq=\"1\"></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:6px;padding-left:16px\"><span style=\"color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">2</span> <span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">A young child cannot come in here alone.</span> <span data-mcq=\"2\"></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:6px;padding-left:16px\"><span style=\"color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">3</span> <span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">You cannot swim here today.</span> <span data-mcq=\"3\"></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:6px;padding-left:16px\"><span style=\"color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">4</span> <span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">Only people who work here may go in.</span> <span data-mcq=\"4\"></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:6px;padding-left:16px\"><span style=\"color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">5</span> <span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">You cannot leave your car here.</span> <span data-mcq=\"5\"></span></p><table class=\"bk\"><tr><td style=\"background:#127D80;width:92px;border:0;vertical-align:middle\"><p style=\"text-align:center;margin:0\"><span style=\"font-weight:700;color:#fff;font-size:11pt\">PART 2</span></p></td><td style=\"border:0;border-bottom:1px solid #127D80;vertical-align:middle\"><p style=\"margin:0\"><span style=\"font-weight:700;color:#0B5456;font-size:11pt\">Questions 6\u201310 \u00b7 the right word</span></p></td></tr></table><p style=\"margin-bottom:8px\"><span style=\"font-style:italic;color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">Read the sentences about a day at the market and choose the correct answer for each gap.</span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:6px;padding-left:16px\"><span style=\"color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">6</span> <span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">Aziz went to the market early to \u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026 some fruit.</span> <span data-mcq=\"6\"></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:6px;padding-left:16px\"><span style=\"color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">7</span> <span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">He \u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026 his bag at home, so he carried everything in his arms.</span> <span data-mcq=\"7\"></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:6px;padding-left:16px\"><span style=\"color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">8</span> <span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">The apples were very \u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026 , so he bought two kilos.</span> <span data-mcq=\"8\"></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:6px;padding-left:16px\"><span style=\"color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">9</span> <span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">A woman \u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026 him the way to the bus stop.</span> <span data-mcq=\"9\"></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:6px;padding-left:16px\"><span style=\"color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">10</span> <span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">He was \u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026 when he got home, so he drank a glass of water.</span> <span data-mcq=\"10\"></span></p><table class=\"bk\"><tr><td style=\"background:#127D80;width:92px;border:0;vertical-align:middle\"><p style=\"text-align:center;margin:0\"><span style=\"font-weight:700;color:#fff;font-size:11pt\">PART 3</span></p></td><td style=\"border:0;border-bottom:1px solid #127D80;vertical-align:middle\"><p style=\"margin:0\"><span style=\"font-weight:700;color:#0B5456;font-size:11pt\">Questions 11\u201315 \u00b7 the article</span></p></td></tr></table><p style=\"margin-bottom:8px\"><span style=\"font-style:italic;color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">Read the article about Samir and answer the questions. For each question, mark A, B or C on the answer sheet.</span></p><table class=\"bk\"><tr><td style=\"background:#fff;border:1px solid #127D80;padding:10px 12px\"><p style=\"margin-bottom:4px\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\"><b>THE MAN WHO MENDS BICYCLES</b></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:4px\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">Samir Aliyev is thirty years old and he mends bicycles in a small shop near the station. He works alone, and on a busy afternoon fifteen customers bring him a bicycle.</span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:4px\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">Samir did not plan to do this work. He studied computers at college for two years and then worked in an office in the city centre. He was not happy there. He sat at a computer all day, and he says he was always tired, even at the weekend.</span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:4px\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">One winter his own bicycle broke. He carried it to an old man in his street and watched him mend it. It was interesting, and he went back the next week, and the week afterwards. Six months later the old man asked him an important question: did he want to work together?</span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:4px\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">The old man is not well now and stays at home, and Samir has the shop. He opens at eight in the morning and closes at six, and he earns less money than he did in the office. He does not mind. He says he sleeps beautifully, and his favourite part of the job is seeing the same customers every week.</span></p></td></tr></table><p style=\"margin-bottom:6px;padding-left:16px\"><span style=\"color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">11</span> <span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">Samir studied</span> <span data-mcq=\"11\"></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:6px;padding-left:16px\"><span style=\"color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">12</span> <span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">In the office, Samir was</span> <span data-mcq=\"12\"></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:6px;padding-left:16px\"><span style=\"color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">13</span> <span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">Samir first met the old man when</span> <span data-mcq=\"13\"></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:6px;padding-left:16px\"><span style=\"color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">14</span> <span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">The old man does not work now because</span> <span data-mcq=\"14\"></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:6px;padding-left:16px\"><span style=\"color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">15</span> <span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">Samir says that now he</span> <span data-mcq=\"15\"></span></p><table class=\"bk\"><tr><td style=\"background:#127D80;width:92px;border:0;vertical-align:middle\"><p style=\"text-align:center;margin:0\"><span style=\"font-weight:700;color:#fff;font-size:11pt\">PART 4</span></p></td><td style=\"border:0;border-bottom:1px solid #127D80;vertical-align:middle\"><p style=\"margin:0\"><span style=\"font-weight:700;color:#0B5456;font-size:11pt\">Questions 16\u201320 \u00b7 the grammar</span></p></td></tr></table><p style=\"margin-bottom:8px\"><span style=\"font-style:italic;color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">Read the article about bees and answer the questions. For each question, mark A, B or C on the answer sheet.</span></p><table class=\"bk\"><tr><td style=\"background:#fff;border:1px solid #127D80;padding:10px 12px\"><p style=\"margin-bottom:4px\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\"><b>BEES</b></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:4px\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">A bee is a small insect, 16 \u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026 it is very important to farmers. Bees travel from flower to flower, and 17 \u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026 this way they help fruit and vegetables to grow. A single bee can visit five thousand flowers in one afternoon. Bees live together in large groups, and one group can have sixty thousand bees 18 \u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026 it. There are 19 \u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026 bees in the world today than there were fifty years ago, and scientists 20 \u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026 worried about this. Farmers are worried too, because without bees many of our favourite vegetables would disappear.</span></p></td></tr></table><p style=\"margin-bottom:6px;padding-left:16px\"><span style=\"color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">16</span> <span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\"></span> <span data-mcq=\"16\"></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:6px;padding-left:16px\"><span style=\"color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">17</span> <span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\"></span> <span data-mcq=\"17\"></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:6px;padding-left:16px\"><span style=\"color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">18</span> <span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\"></span> <span data-mcq=\"18\"></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:6px;padding-left:16px\"><span style=\"color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">19</span> <span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\"></span> <span data-mcq=\"19\"></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:6px;padding-left:16px\"><span style=\"color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">20</span> <span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\"></span> <span data-mcq=\"20\"></span></p><table class=\"bk\"><tr><td style=\"background:#127D80;width:92px;border:0;vertical-align:middle\"><p style=\"text-align:center;margin:0\"><span style=\"font-weight:700;color:#fff;font-size:11pt\">PART 5</span></p></td><td style=\"border:0;border-bottom:1px solid #127D80;vertical-align:middle\"><p style=\"margin:0\"><span style=\"font-weight:700;color:#0B5456;font-size:11pt\">Questions 21\u201325 \u00b7 one word in each gap</span></p></td></tr></table><p style=\"margin-bottom:8px\"><span style=\"font-style:italic;color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">Read the text. Think of the word which fits each gap. Write ONE word for each gap.</span></p><table class=\"bk\"><tr><td style=\"background:#fff;border:1px solid #127D80;padding:10px 12px\"><p style=\"margin-bottom:4px\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\"><b>Dear Sir or Madam,</b></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:4px\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">I (Example: saw) your advertisement for a Saturday job in the bookshop. I am seventeen years old and I am still 21 \u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026 school. I have worked in a shop before, 22 \u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026 only for two weeks in the summer. Could you tell me what time the shop opens 23 \u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026 Saturdays? I am free all day.</span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:4px\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">Yours faithfully,<br>Oybek Yusupov</span></p></td></tr></table><table class=\"bk\"><tr><td style=\"background:#fff;border:1px solid #127D80;padding:10px 12px\"><p style=\"margin-bottom:4px\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\"><b>Dear Mr Yusupov,</b></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:4px\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">Thank you 24 \u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026 your letter. We would like to meet you next week. Please come 25 \u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026 the shop on Tuesday at four o&#x27;clock and ask for Mrs Hill. The job is from nine until five.</span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:4px\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">Yours sincerely,<br>Anna Hill</span></p></td></tr></table><p style=\"margin-bottom:6px;padding-left:16px\"><span style=\"color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">21</span> <span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">Write ONE word for gap 21.</span> <input class=\"bk-blank\" data-q=\"21\" style=\"width:150px\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocapitalize=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\"></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:6px;padding-left:16px\"><span style=\"color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">22</span> <span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">Write ONE word for gap 22.</span> <input class=\"bk-blank\" data-q=\"22\" style=\"width:150px\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocapitalize=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\"></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:6px;padding-left:16px\"><span style=\"color:#6E6E6E;font-size:10pt\">23</span> <span style=\"font-size:10.5pt\">Write ONE word for gap 23.</span> <input class=\"bk-blank\" data-q=\"23\" style=\"width:150px\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocapitalize=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\"></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:6px;padding-left:16px\"><span 